+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2G2AGVRZPBP3VH8FNAYH46V","supersedes":"fnd_01M2G2AGVRZPBP3VH8FNAYH46V","recordedAt":"2026-09-15T02:47:35Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"MCP HTTP transport endpoint ships with no authentication, rate limiting or idempotency controls by default","description":"src/transports/mcpHttpServer.ts:306-419 exposes POST/GET/DELETE /mcp with no authentication by default: the only built-in mechanism is exact-match validation of the operator-configured httpHeaders map, which defaults to an empty object (src/common/config/userConfig.ts:136-143: httpHeaders: z.object({}).loose().default({})), so the middleware (lines 308-318) validates nothing; snippet: for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(this.userConfig.httpHeaders)) { const header = req.headers[key.toLowerCase()]; if (!header || header !== value) ... }. There is no per-request authorisation of tool calls, no rate limiter, no 429 or 409 handling, and no TLS termination in the express app. With externallyManagedSessions=true any request may supply an arbitrary mcp-session-id header and get a session without authentication (lines 336-355), after which every enabled tool (find, aggregate, insert-many, update-many, delete-many, drop-database, atlas tools) is callable against the client-data and order stores. The optional monitoring server exposes /health and /metrics unauthenticated too (src/transports/monitoringServer.ts:53-79). Deployed to prod (eks-prod-mumbai, exposure partner, data classes pii and financial) any in-cluster caller can read client data; no gateway policy (x-kong-plugin, x-amazon-apigateway-auth, Istio RequestAuthentication) exists in this repo. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S17. DPDP Rule 6(1)(b) (commences 2027-05-13) is a readiness mapping. SLA topic: patch-sla. Commit aaa72a040db4c32f3d6488d5e28e2892a68e9ee0.\n\nRefutation: evidence lens not refuted (Not refuted: every substantive claim verifies in files I opened m