nded database/collection z.string(); insertMany.ts:22-26 documents array without maxItems; export.ts:16 and searchKnowledge.ts:9-14 unbounded strings; constants.ts:15-17 stdio 50 MiB 'informational only' with no enforcement anywhere in stdio.ts, while mcpHttpServer.ts:307's 100 KiB express.json cap is the only enforcement — disclosed accurately by the finding); the SARIF export exists, is valid SARIF 2.1.0 from maxwell-schema-auditor 1.0.0, and defines rule SCH-API-02 at defaultSeverity medium on the stated sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S2 basis with the candidate's exact regulatoryRefs; severity medium equals PR.IP.S2's catalog defaultSeverity (sebi-cscrf-2024.catalog.json line 3677), dpdp-rules-2025:Act-8(3) exists in its catalog as a pre-13-May-2027 readiness control whose guidance names probe-schemas (matching the 'readiness mapping' wording), and all four instruments are in instruments.json; the repo is the deployed source for qa/prod (repo record pinned at the cited commit, env iac, bicep deploys mongodb/mongodb-mcp-server:1.11.0 built by this repo's CI) with no overlay, ignore file or central validation overriding the per-field gap; and the fingerprint is byte-identical to the open ledger finding fnd_01M2G2AGX1GZ9THG6HJ1VPP1EP for the same SCH-API-02 result at src/tools/args.ts, so this is the designed fingerprint-based re-run update rather than a duplicate (note the earlier run mapped the same fingerprint to PR.AA.S17/high, which the ledger keeper's supersession resolves); the only bytes I could not read are the gitignored export's results[] entry (single-line file truncated at char 2000, grep skips gitignored paths) and its sha256, both corroborated by the readable rule metadata, the identical prior-run fingerprint and the checkout itself — so no check under this lens fails.); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (Every check verifiable in the workspace passed: sebi-cscrf-2024 binds example-co (active mid-size-re stock-broker and depository-participant, jurisdiction