ord echoed in the success response at 89-96 with the line-93 snippet verbatim, keychain registration at 84-87 that only feeds redaction of error messages (tool.ts:819), telemetry (telemetry.ts:342-348) and logs (loggerBase.ts:66) while the success path through invoke/appendUIResource performs no redaction), the stated compensating controls are real and accurately described (atlas-create-db-user is on the default confirmationRequiredTools list at userConfig.ts:83 and the prompt masks the password at line 109), nothing overrides the gap (deploy/ contains no readOnly or disabledTools settings), the repo is deployed in prod (partner exposure), qa and dev per env/*.json iac entries, the pinned commit aaa72a040db4c32f3d6488d5e28e2892a68e9ee0 matches the repo record, and severity high equals the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S6 (sebi-cscrf-2024.catalog.json:2399) so no lower severity is warranted; note for the keeper: the ledger already holds this exact fingerprint as open finding fnd_01M2G2AGTH64FMR4XR77ZAJH7B with the same target and ruleId (narrower location 84-96), so this append should update/supersede that record rather than create a second one.); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (All five cited instruments apply to example-co and are ordered Indian-first (sebi-cscrf-2024 is the primary instrument for a mid-size SEBI RE per details.json entityTypes stock-broker/depository-participant and active mid-size-re registrations; dpdp-rules-2025 is in frameworksInScope and covers stock-broker; owasp-asvs-5.0 and nist-800-53-r5 are cross-sector with empty applicability), controlIds sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S6, sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S1 and dpdp-rules-2025:6(1) all exist in their catalog files and cover the credential-echo gap (PR.AA.S6's guidance names probe-schemas checking credentials and probe-schemas is in its probeWorkflows; 6(1) is the umbrella safeguards control with probe-schemas in its probeWorkflows and ledger precedent on this very app), and severi