+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"observation","id":"obs_01M2KBJW49XR5GDXP2S1CPV67A","recordedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","companyId":"example-co","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S17"],"title":"V8 Authorization: single-privilege gateway; the MongoDB user is the only authorization boundary","description":"There is no per-caller principal, role or tenant model: every caller that reaches /mcp gets the full registered tool surface and the full privileges of the configured MongoDB connection (readOnly and disabledTools are global server config evaluated at registration, src/tools/tool.ts:757-783), and the connect tool can repoint the gateway at any MongoDB URI. Atlas tools register only when API credentials exist (src/tools/atlas/atlasTool.ts:12-17). No per-object ownership exists, so no IDOR surface exists; but because the transport authenticates nobody (V4 finding), every reachable caller is fully privileged against the pii/financial stores - authorization cannot be satisfied by the code alone.","methods":["execute-scr"],"subjects":[{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"}],"collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","expiresAt":"2026-10-15T19:42:44Z","result":"partial","evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/tools/tool.ts","sha256":"710324a9ac625baf40b786107520129c3672ec10deb7884f79e7202f370234f1","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"verifyAllowed uses global config only, lines 757-783"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/tools/atlas/atlasTool.ts","sha256":"36b5e190889217251fb268c680276bc4c9326507ab7ea80ddb226f43a56d8e46","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"Atlas tools gated on credentials presence, lines 12-17"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/common/session.ts","sha256":"ed09089a275430441c110da1d42e675103e5e9e9d4969b69acce90ada7b7d111","collectedAt":"2026-