+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"observation","id":"obs_01M2KBJW4ADD28CSBXK9A65348","recordedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","companyId":"example-co","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S8"],"title":"V16 Security Logging and Error Handling: redaction present; audit trail carries no caller identity","description":"All loggers redact messages and attributes against session and root keychain secrets before writing to disk, mcp or stderr (src/common/logging/loggerBase.ts:13-67), and tool errors returned to clients are redacted with no stack traces (src/tools/tool.ts:813-829; src/transports/mcpHttpServer.ts:414-436). Disk logs rotate after 30 days (src/common/logging/diskLogger.ts:17-44) while the prod SIEM retains 365 days per env metadata. Partial: because the transport authenticates nobody, events cannot be attributed to a caller identity, source IP or correlation id (only a server-side sessionId), user-controlled strings (export names, error text) enter log context fields without newline neutralisation (CWE-117), and there are no authn/authz security events to log at all - the audit trail expected for privileged actions does not exist.","methods":["execute-scr"],"subjects":[{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"}],"collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","expiresAt":"2026-10-15T19:42:44Z","result":"partial","evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/common/logging/loggerBase.ts","sha256":"720eb5f8d68a38a516b73c53a0034bce591741375fac5840f783b3697c6c0a98","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"redactIfNecessary on every log path, lines 13-67"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/common/logging/diskLogger.ts","sha256":"09227ed56dc404e8b75c8fa43268dd96a40147b3c7fa88eeb34a444d5ec13603","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"MongoLogManager 30-day retention, lines 17-44"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/transports/mcpHttpServer.ts","sha256":"1f3fb9ae5a29c80b24b68ab25a7f363ba6a2d4e095b6cfa1747452dea56861f4","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"generic error response, no stack traces, lines 414-436"},{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/opencode/ses_f5966a873ffeW6ABw4BrDNZjnn.execute-scr.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","sha256":"1c38ee55b22f898a973cc3b4d9aefcf12185ed448e2bd5602df2ec0d371d91c6","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"pass result asvs-v16-log-redaction (index 5)"}],"tags":["scr","scr:v16"],"provenance":{"harness":"opencode","generatedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","sessionId":"ses_f5966a873ffeW6ABw4BrDNZjnn","runId":"run_01M2GDZ3Q3S5WYCB3MV02QJXZ1","workflow":"execute-scr","agent":"soc-ledger-keeper"}}
+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2KBJW4AHE221KPTRV1G60YC","recordedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"mcp-gateway/mongodb-mcp-server: Human-confirmation gate for destructive MCP tools fails open for clients without elicitation support","description":"ASVS 5.0 L2 scope with agent-code lenses (LLM06, ASI02). destructive tools (drop-database, drop-collection, delete-many, drop-index, atlas-create-db-user, atlas-create-access-list, atlas-streams-manage, atlas-streams-teardown) are listed in confirmationRequiredTools by default (src/common/config/userConfig.ts:79-94) and ToolBase.invoke asks Elicitation.requestConfirmation before executing them (src/tools/tool.ts:491-513, 609-615); requestConfirmation returns true immediately when the MCP client does not declare the elicitation capability (src/elicitation.ts:30-33), so any client that omits that capability executes destructive operations against the pii/financial stores with no human approval. ExampleCo sdlc policy lists human-approval-for-writes as its prompt-injection control, and this is the code path meant to enforce it. Severity high from the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S3 (least privilege and segregation of duties); no CVSS computed because the caller already reaches the API - the defect removes a required human control rather than crossing a privilege boundary. SARIF result index 1.\n\nData flow: tools/call on MCP HTTP transport -> ToolBase.invoke requiresConfirmation (tool.ts:491-513) -> verifyConfirmed -> Elicitation.requestConfirmation returns true when supportsElicitation() is false (elicitation.ts:31-33) -> destructive tool executes against MongoDB\n\nExploit scenario: An MCP client (for example a compromised or prompt-injected agent runtime) sends initialize without the elicitation capability, then calls tools/call drop-database; the server skips the confirmation entirely and drops the database with no human ever seeing a prompt.\n\nImpact: On the partner-exposed prod gateway every confirmation-required destructive operation is effectively unattended for clients that omit one capability flag, defeating the human-approval-for-writes control of the company AI coding policy for a system holding pii and financial data; a prompt-injected agent (LLM06/ASI02) can destroy or rewrite client data before a human notices. Catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S3 is high; recorded as context, not as an uplift.\n\nRemediation: Fail closed: in Elicitation.requestConfirmation, return false (refuse the call) when the client does not support elicitation while a confirmation-required tool is invoked; optionally add a config flag to make confirmations mandatory for destructive tools regardless of client capability, and log every confirmation request and outcome as a security event.\n\nSource: maxwell-secure-code-reviewer agent analysis (execute-scr) at pinned commit aaa72a040db4c32f3d6488d5e28e2892a68e9ee0; no scanner SARIF log exists for this target.","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S3"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.AA.S3"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-llm-top10-2025","controlId":"LLM06"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-agentic-top10-2026","controlId":"ASI02"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"src/elicitation.ts","startLine":30,"endLine":33},"fingerprint":"8ecab0bd0359448e815853d574c6ee79b09f539cdae6e54c38985a94f97274fe","source":{"kind":"agent-analysis","ruleId":"asvs-v2-confirmation-fail-open","tool":"secure-code-reviewer"},"status":"open","slaDueAt":"2026-09-22T19:42:44Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.MA.S3","topic":"patch-sla","severity":"high","days":7},"relatedObservationIds":["obs_01M2KBJW49PYVZW02VTCZBQA9F"],"firstSeenAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/elicitation.ts","sha256":"8251845031dac9ef4d453e1251995c4e72ad1cf2c889a920d584fec8d7bb867a","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"requestConfirmation returns true without elicitation support, lines 30-33"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/tools/tool.ts","sha256":"710324a9ac625baf40b786107520129c3672ec10deb7884f79e7202f370234f1","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"invoke/verifyConfirmed confirmation gate, lines 487-515 and 609-615"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/common/config/userConfig.ts","sha256":"a8ec53f96221243921f5010ec927834efba983d9e272413452523af72a6c3158","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"confirmationRequiredTools defaults include drop-database, lines 79-94"},{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/opencode/ses_f5966a873ffeW6ABw4BrDNZjnn.execute-scr.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","sha256":"1c38ee55b22f898a973cc3b4d9aefcf12185ed448e2bd5602df2ec0d371d91c6","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"result index 1, fingerprint 8ecab0bd"}],"tags":["scr","scr:v2","cwe:cwe-285"],"provenance":{"harness":"opencode","generatedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","sessionId":"ses_f5966a873ffeW6ABw4BrDNZjnn","runId":"run_01M2GDZ3Q3S5WYCB3MV02QJXZ1","workflow":"execute-scr","agent":"soc-ledger-keeper"}}
+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2KBJW4A8E9GMQHZT9F9WTAG","recordedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"mcp-gateway/mongodb-mcp-server: Telemetry enabled by default sends machine and usage identifiers to the MongoDB cloud with no consent gate","description":"ASVS 5.0 L2 scope, data-protection lens. Telemetry defaults to enabled (src/common/config/userConfig.ts:113-117); the Telemetry pipeline batches events every 30 seconds and posts them, after keychain redaction of secret values, to the MongoDB cloud endpoint api/private/unauth/telemetry/events under https://cloud.mongodb.com (src/common/atlas/apiClient.ts:170-236), with a fallback to the unauthenticated endpoint whenever the Atlas token is absent or rejected. Events carry device_id sourced from node-machine-id machineId(true) (src/helpers/deviceId.ts:20-24), session_id, tool names, durations, result status, Atlas project and org ids and auth types (src/telemetry/telemetry.ts:339-352; src/tools/atlas/atlasTool.ts:97-129); the only opt-outs are the DO_NOT_TRACK environment variable or telemetry disabled in config, neither set by deploy/aws/Dockerfile. No consent notice, purpose artefact or processor agreement is consulted before this external disclosure from an IN-residency deployment. Severity medium from the catalog defaultSeverity of dpdp-rules-2025:3 (standalone, itemised consent notice). Confidence likely: the egress and defaults are confirmed in code, but whether the machine identifier constitutes personal data and any DPA with MongoDB are not visible in the repo. SARIF result index 2.\n\nData flow: tool/server events -> Telemetry.emitEvents (telemetry.ts:209-215) -> sendEvents with redacted properties (telemetry.ts:339-352) -> ApiClient.sendUnauthEvents POST to https://cloud.mongodb.com api/private/unauth/telemetry/events (apiClient.ts:218-236), device_id from node-machine-id (deviceId.ts:20-24)\n\nExploit scenario: Deploy the shipped defaults (deploy/aws/Dockerfile sets no MDB_MCP_TELEMETRY) on the prod gateway; from the first tool call the deployment continuously emits the EKS node machine identifier, session ids, tool usage and Atlas project ids to MongoDB servers outside the company boundary, with no notice to or consent artefact for the company and no processor agreement visible in the repo.\n\nImpact: Default-on external disclosure of persistent device identifiers and gateway usage metadata from a system processing pii and financial data for an Indian SEBI/RBI-regulated entity with dataResidency IN; DPDP Rules 2025 require an itemised consent notice before such sharing and the SDLC secrets policy expects AWS Secrets Manager for credentials, not ad-hoc third-party telemetry. Catalog defaultSeverity of dpdp-rules-2025:3 is medium; recorded as context, not as an uplift.\n\nRemediation: Set MDB_MCP_TELEMETRY=disabled (or DO_NOT_TRACK) in the mcp-gateway deployments and consider changing the upstream default to disabled for enterprise deployments; if telemetry is retained, document a purpose and processor agreement with MongoDB, hash the machine identifier, and gate emission on a recorded consent decision.\n\nSource: maxwell-secure-code-reviewer agent analysis (execute-scr) at pinned commit aaa72a040db4c32f3d6488d5e28e2892a68e9ee0; no scanner SARIF log exists for this target.","severity":"medium","confidence":"likely","controlIds":["dpdp-rules-2025:3"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"MeitY","instrument":"dpdp-rules-2025","controlId":"3"},{"regulator":"ISO","instrument":"iso-27001-2022","controlId":"A.5.34"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"src/common/config/userConfig.ts","startLine":113,"endLine":117},"fingerprint":"6a374db17afda45b8b0560c31bb870f6d0b773b7f91ffe3ae2b6cd16de3fde47","source":{"kind":"agent-analysis","ruleId":"asvs-v14-consent-purpose","tool":"secure-code-reviewer"},"status":"open","slaDueAt":"2026-09-29T19:42:44Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-c