r image"},{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/opencode/run_01M2GDZ3Q3S5WYCB3MV02QJXZ1.probe-sdlc.example-co.company.sarif.export.json","sha256":"d787ca478c2edd23878ffc79ec44a21980d7292eabcca6dd2e94c63491893a56","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T20:48:43Z"}],"tags":["sdlc","ssdf:ps-3"],"provenance":{"harness":"opencode","generatedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","sessionId":"453ecc6e-1346-418f-a2c0-1bfcead851c3","runId":"run_01M2GDZ3Q3S5WYCB3MV02QJXZ1","workflow":"execute-scr","agent":"soc-ledger-keeper"},"description":"dependencyPolicy.sbomRequired is false (line 66) although sebi-cscrf-2024 GV.SC.S5 requires an SBOM for all core and critical software and the company is a SEBI mid-size RE. mcp-gateway is the only application backing the order-routing critical function (details.json criticalFunctions) and its qa and prod environments run docker.io/mongodb/mongodb-mcp-server images (applications/mcp-gateway/README.md; registry images built by CI), yet no SBOM exists: applications/mcp-gateway/images/ and applications/db-models/images/ do not exist and no *.cdx.json is anywhere in the workspace. The CI docker build attaches an sbom attestation to the pushed image (docker-publish.yml line 87) but nothing is retained on file and the policy sets no sbomFormat.\n\nImpact: No component inventory exists for the image running the order-routing critical function, so a disclosure like Log4Shell or an upstream supply-chain compromise cannot be matched against what actually runs in prod; a direct CSCRF GV.SC.S5 breach for a mid-size RE.\n\nRemediation: Set sbomRequired true with sbomFormat CycloneDX in sdlc/policy.json; export the image SBOM at build (the buildx sbom: true attestation already carries it) and file it as applications/mcp-gateway/images/<imageId>.cdx.json; capture the image records via refresh-apps."}
