+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2KM42DZDZSFHCN7YYBM94V2","recordedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"Dev environment retains logs only 30 days against the CERT-In 180-day baseline","description":"The dev-tier environment record applications/mcp-gateway/env/dev.json declares observability.logsRetentionDays 30 with logsInIndia true (lines 14-17), 150 days below the CERT-In Direction iv requirement to retain ICT system logs for 180 days within India. The dev tier is the shared first stage of the release path (sdlc/policy.json releaseProcess.environmentsOrder [dev, qa, prod]) hosted on the developer-laptop fleet (hosting.accountRef developer-laptops, probeAccess method docker-socket); qa already retains 180 days and prod 365, so only dev falls short. The record is the evidence itself; the file literally shows the value. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of cert-in-directions-2022 Dir-iv (high).\n\nImpact: Dev-tier activity - including the developer-laptop fleet that builds this order-routing-critical application - becomes unavailable for investigation 150 days before the regulatory baseline, losing dev-stage evidence for CERT-In incident timelines and SEBI CSCRF audits; the same application's qa and prod tiers already meet the baseline, making dev the only gap. SLA topic: log-retention.\n\nRemediation: Centralise dev-laptop logs into the same India-resident pipeline used by qa (which already retains 180 days) and raise the dev tier record to at least 180 days.","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["cert-in-directions-2022:Dir-iv"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"CERT-In","instrument":"cert-in-directions-2022","controlId":"Dir-iv"},{"regulator":"NIST","instrument":"nist-800-53-r5","controlId":"AU-11"}],"target":{"type":"environment","appId":"mcp-gateway","envId":"dev"},"location":{"path":"applications/mcp-gateway/env/dev.json","startLine":14,"endLine":17},"fingerprint":"9996cd0e92b4ebc4ac0ff208635a5e